{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310839,"nonce":"WciUhvZ/qcEKxUR8rioUZX/DYIo=","title":"Chat-template prompt wrapping landed for llama-chat (commit b041ba0). BPETokenizer.encode now recognises registered specials inline ...","message":"Three pieces, single commit (b041ba0):\n\n1. **BPETokenizer.encode → special-aware**. Walks the input, at each position tries longest-special prefix match (against `specialNames:Array\u003cString\u003e` mirror of the StringMap keys). Matched specials emit their atomic id, runs between specials route through the renamed private `encodeBPE` helper.\n\n2. **GGUFTokenizer.build → register chat specials**. After the existing `tokenizer.ggml.bos_token_id` / `eos_token_id` registration, scan an array of `\u003c|eot_id|\u003e`, `\u003c|start_header_id|\u003e`, `\u003c|end_header_id|\u003e`, `\u003c|begin_of_text|\u003e`, `\u003c|end_of_text|\u003e` and try `vocab.lookup(name)` for each. Idempotent against the by-metadata path.\n\n3. **Main.hx → chat-template wrap**. If `tok.specialId(\"\u003c|start_header_id|\u003e\") \u003e= 0`, build\n   ```\n   \u003c|begin_of_text|\u003e\u003c|start_header_id|\u003euser\u003c|end_header_id|\u003e\\n\\n\n   {prompt}\u003c|eot_id|\u003e\n   \u003c|start_header_id|\u003eassistant\u003c|end_header_id|\u003e\\n\\n\n   ```\n   and feed that to `GenerationLoop.generate` instead of the raw prompt. Otherwise pass-through.\n\n\n`TopPSampler` insertion-sorts the FULL vocab per token. For Llama 3 with 128k tokens that's ~16B comparisons per token → minutes per token. Tried switching but had to back out. Partial-sort / top-K-then-nucleus is the natural follow-up; meanwhile greedy + chat template avoids the repetition loop because the template gives the model a clean EOS exit point.\n\n\nLlama 3.2 1B Instruct Q4_K_M, prompt `\"What is the capital of France?\"`:\n- **Before chat template** (raw prompt, Argmax): `'a country, and the largest country in which is the most …'` — base-LM continuation\n- **After chat template** (chat-wrapped, Argmax): `'The correct? Unfortunately, I think the capital of the and the I need to build a capital city of the in in in in of'` — chat-style response, factually wrong, still repetition-prone at the tail\n\nSo coherence (in the chat-style sense) is restored; semantic correctness still drifts. Output ends in \"in in in in\" which is the greedy-loop signature, but now happens after a chat-style response rather than from the first token.\n\n\nThe architecture work is done — bmm strides, reshape materialisation, RoPE half-split, enum disambig are all landed. The 1B Instruct picking the wrong tokens for \"What is the capital of France?\" is most likely one of:\n\n1. **Cumulative precision drift** through 16 layers F32. Per-layer hidden-state magnitude vs HF would isolate.\n2. **Q6_K cumulative dequant noise**. Per-block decode matches Python ref; cumulative drift across 1M+ blocks of token_embd unverified.\n3. **Llama 3.2 1B is just weak.** The 1B Instruct is a small model and known for shaky factual recall; 3B+ would be a better coherence sanity check if memory allows.\n4. **Tokenizer pre-split missing.** llama.cpp / OpenAI pre-tokenize via a regex that splits contractions and runs of letters/digits/punctuation before BPE. We currently run BPE on the whole input. For chat-template strings with mixed punctuation this can produce 1-2 different tokens vs reference. Long flagged in BPETokenizer.hx but not yet implemented.\n\n\n- Partial-sort TopPSampler (heap-based top-K then nucleus). Goal: \u003c100ms/token on the 128k vocab.\n- Streaming display in Main.hx is buggy — `Sys.print(delta)` prints cumulative not delta because of closure variable capture-by-value semantics on `prevLen`. nTokens stays 0 for same reason.\n- Pre-tokenization regex pass before BPE.\n- Per-layer magnitude trace vs HF reference (the diagnostic recipe queued from [[project-llama-chat-coherence-status]]).\n\n\n- [[project-llama-chat-coherence-phase-c]] — bmm + reshape + RoPE + enum disambig that made the model coherent at all. This memory is the chat-mode follow-up.\n- [[bugs-bpe-utf8-codepoint-walk]] — UTF-8 decoder fix; precondition for the chat template work (special-token strings round-trip cleanly).\n- [[bugs-stringmap-null-get]] — why the new code uses a parallel `specialNames` array instead of `specials.keys()`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_llama_chat_chat_template` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}